### ==============================================================================
### Aegis Claims Platform - Comprehensive REST Client API Test Suite
### Compatible with: VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client, Chrome Extensions
### Architecture: Client -> API Gateway (:8080) -> Eureka Discovery (:9000) -> Services
### Database: PostgreSQL (policy_db, claim_db, approval_db)
### ==============================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080
@eurekaUrl = http://localhost:9000

### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 1: AUTHENTICATION & JWT TOKEN EXTRACTION
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Login as ADMIN (Returns JWT with ROLE_ADMIN)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### Extracted Admin Token
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}


### 1.2 Login as REGULAR USER (Returns JWT with ROLE_USER)
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "user123"
}

### Extracted User Token
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.token}}


### 1.3 Failed Login with Invalid Password (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "WrongPassword999!"
}


### 1.4 Failed Login with Non-Existent User (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nonexistent_officer",
  "password": "password123"
}


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 2: POLICY MANAGEMENT (PostgreSQL Persistence via API Gateway)
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 List All Policies from PostgreSQL (ADMIN / USER)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.2 Get Active Auto Policy (Bruce Wayne - $75,000 Coverage)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.3 Get Active Health Policy (Clark Kent - $100,000 Coverage)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.4 Get Active Property Policy (Diana Prince - $250,000 Coverage)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.5 Get Expired Auto Policy (Victor Stone - $30,000 Coverage - Expired 2025)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/6
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.6 Query Non-Existent Policy (Expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.7 Create New Corporate Fleet Policy (ADMIN Only - Expected: 201 Created)
# @name createPolicy
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-2026-CORP-888",
  "customerName": "Queen Industries Cargo",
  "policyType": "COMMERCIAL",
  "coverageAmount": 600000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 2.8 Create Policy with Duplicate Policy Number (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-2026-AUTO-001",
  "customerName": "Imposter Bruce",
  "policyType": "AUTO",
  "coverageAmount": 50000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 2.9 Create Policy with Invalid Negative Coverage (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-2026-INVALID-001",
  "customerName": "Invalid Applicant",
  "policyType": "AUTO",
  "coverageAmount": -25000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 2.10 Update Existing Policy Coverage and Term (ADMIN Only - Expected: 200 OK)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-2026-AUTO-001",
  "customerName": "Bruce Wayne",
  "policyType": "COMPREHENSIVE",
  "coverageAmount": 85000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 2.11 Validate Active Policy #1 (Expected: valid = true, active = true)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/1/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.12 Validate Expired Policy #6 (Expected: valid = false, status = EXPIRED)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/6/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 2.13 Delete Policy by ID (ADMIN Only - Expected: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/8
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 3: CLAIM LIFECYCLE & STATE MACHINE SCENARIOS
### (Triggers Spring RestClient inter-service calls across Eureka & Gateway)
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Scenario A: Auto-Approved Auto Claim (Within Coverage Limit)
# Evaluates $15,000 against $85,000 coverage on Policy 1 -> AUTO-APPROVED
# @name submitApprovedClaim
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-auto-approved-auto-01

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "customerName": "Bruce Wayne",
  "claimAmount": 15000.00,
  "description": "Front fender and sensor assembly repair",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-10"
}


### 3.2 Scenario B: Auto-Approved Health Claim (Clark Kent - Policy 2)
# Evaluates $8,500 against $100,000 coverage on Policy 2 -> AUTO-APPROVED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-auto-approved-health-02

{
  "policyId": 2,
  "customerName": "Clark Kent",
  "claimAmount": 8500.00,
  "description": "Annual specialized medical diagnostics and lab analysis",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-12"
}


### 3.3 Scenario C: Auto-Approved Property Claim (Diana Prince - Policy 3)
# Evaluates $50,000 against $250,000 coverage on Policy 3 -> AUTO-APPROVED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-auto-approved-property-03

{
  "policyId": 3,
  "customerName": "Diana Prince",
  "claimAmount": 50000.00,
  "description": "Roof restoration after thunderstorm damage",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-14"
}


### 3.4 Scenario D: Claim Exceeding Policy Coverage (REJECTED by Adjudication Engine)
# Policy 4 has $15,000 cap. Submitting $45,000 claim causes Approval Service rejection.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-excess-rejected-04

{
  "policyId": 4,
  "customerName": "Barry Allen",
  "claimAmount": 45000.00,
  "description": "Supersonic velocity luggage loss exceeding coverage",
  "claimDate": "2026-06-15"
}


### 3.5 Scenario E: Claim on Expired Policy (REJECTED at Intake Validation)
# Policy 6 has status EXPIRED (2025). Rejected during Policy Service check.
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-expired-rejected-05

{
  "policyId": 6,
  "customerName": "Victor Stone",
  "claimAmount": 8000.00,
  "description": "Hardware diagnostics claim on lapsed policy",
  "claimDate": "2026-07-20"
}


### 3.6 Scenario F: Claim on Non-Existent Policy (REJECTED: Policy Not Found)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-nonexistent-policy-06

{
  "policyId": 9999,
  "customerName": "Unknown Claimant",
  "claimAmount": 5000.00,
  "description": "Claim on unregistered ghost policy",
  "claimDate": "2026-07-22"
}


### 3.7 Scenario G: Input Validation Failure - Negative Claim Amount (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "customerName": "Bruce Wayne",
  "claimAmount": -500.00,
  "description": "Negative amount test",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-10"
}


### 3.8 Scenario H: Input Validation Failure - Missing Customer Name (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "customerName": "",
  "claimAmount": 2500.00,
  "description": "Missing customer name test",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-10"
}


### 3.9 Scenario I: Idempotency Protection Re-Submission
# Re-submitting with identical Idempotency-Key returns existing claim with zero duplicate records
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: claim-auto-approved-auto-01

{
  "policyId": 1,
  "customerName": "Bruce Wayne",
  "claimAmount": 15000.00,
  "description": "Front fender and sensor assembly repair",
  "claimDate": "2026-05-10"
}


### 3.10 Query All Claims in System
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 3.11 Query Claim Details by ID (e.g. Claim 1)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/claims/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 3.12 Query Complete State Transition Audit Trail (e.g. Claim 1)
# Demonstrates: SUBMITTED -> POLICY_VALIDATED -> UNDER_REVIEW -> APPROVED with timestamps and changedBy
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/claims/1/history
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 3.13 State Machine Terminal State Violation Check (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
# Attempting to transition an already APPROVED claim to REJECTED violates terminal state rules
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/claims/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "REJECTED",
  "reason": "Post-approval reversal attempt (Terminal status violation)"
}


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 4: APPROVAL & UNDERWRITING ENGINE (Approval Service via Gateway)
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Direct Adjudication: Approved Case (Claim Amount <= Coverage Amount)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/evaluate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimId": 801,
  "policyId": 1,
  "claimAmount": 25000.00,
  "coverageAmount": 85000.00,
  "description": "Direct Underwriting Simulation - Approved"
}


### 4.2 Direct Adjudication: Rejected Case (Claim Amount > Coverage Amount)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/evaluate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimId": 802,
  "policyId": 4,
  "claimAmount": 75000.00,
  "coverageAmount": 15000.00,
  "description": "Direct Underwriting Simulation - Exceeds Coverage"
}


### 4.3 Direct Adjudication: Validation Failure (Negative Coverage -> 400 Bad Request)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/evaluate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claimId": 803,
  "policyId": 1,
  "claimAmount": 1000.00,
  "coverageAmount": -5000.00,
  "description": "Invalid negative coverage test"
}


### 4.4 Query Adjudication Decision for Claim 1
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/claim/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 4.5 Query Adjudication Decision by Decision Record ID
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 4.6 List All Historical Adjudication Decisions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 4.7 Query Adjudication for Non-Existent Claim (Expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/approvals/claim/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 5: SECURITY, RBAC & PERIMETER DEFENSE CHECKS
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 RBAC Guard: USER attempting to create a policy (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-UNAUTHORIZED-MUTATION",
  "customerName": "Malicious User",
  "policyType": "AUTO",
  "coverageAmount": 10000.00,
  "startDate": "2026-01-01",
  "endDate": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 5.2 RBAC Guard: USER attempting to delete a policy (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/policies/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 5.3 RBAC Guard: USER attempting to manually override claim status (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/claims/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "APPROVED",
  "reason": "Attempted self-approval"
}


### 5.4 Missing Authorization Header on Protected Endpoint (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/claims


### 5.5 Tampered / Invalid JWT Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.fakeHeader.fakeSignature


### 5.6 Expired JWT Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIiwicm9sZSI6IlJPTEVfVVNFUiIsImlhdCI6MTYwMDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxNjAwMDAwMDEwfQ.tamperedSignature


### 5.7 Non-Bearer Authorization Scheme (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/policies
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=


### ==============================================================================
### SECTION 6: SERVICE DISCOVERY & TOPOLOGY OBSERVABILITY
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 Query All Microservices Registered in Eureka (Port 9000)
GET {{eurekaUrl}}/eureka/apps
Accept: application/json


### 6.2 Check API Gateway Health Endpoint
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json


### 6.3 Check Eureka Discovery Server Health Endpoint
GET {{eurekaUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json
